# ============================================================================
# 📚 LEARNER GUIDE: .dockerignore — What NOT to Copy into Docker Image
# ============================================================================
# WHAT IS .dockerignore?
# ----------------------
# Like .gitignore, but for Docker. It tells `docker build` which files to EXCLUDE
# when copying via `COPY . .` in Dockerfile.
#   - Without it, `COPY . .` would copy EVERYTHING (including .git, node_modules, etc.)
#   - This would make image HUGE and slow, and leak secrets
#
# WHY NEEDED?
# -----------
# - Smaller image (exclude .git, node_modules, logs, etc.)
# - Faster build (less to copy)
# - Security (exclude .env, secrets, etc.)
# - Avoid cache invalidation (if .git changes, COPY . . would invalidate cache)
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
# -------------
# - Each line is a pattern (like .gitignore)
# - `*` = wildcard, `!` = exception (include), `/` = directory
# - Example: `*.log` = ignore all .log files, `!README.md` = but include README.md
#
# FLOW:
# -----
# 1. docker build . → Reads .dockerignore
# 2. For each file, checks if it matches any pattern → If yes, skip it
# 3. Only non-ignored files are sent to Docker daemon and copied via COPY
# 4. Verify: docker build . --progress=plain 2>&1 | grep "transferring context"
# ============================================================================

# Version control — Don't copy git history (huge, not needed in image)
.git
.gitignore
.github  # CI workflows, not needed in image

# Python — Don't copy cache, compiled files, virtual envs
__pycache__  # Python cache (regenerated)
*.pyc        # Compiled Python
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info   # Package metadata
dist/        # Distribution files
build/       # Build artifacts
*.egg
.venv        # Virtual env (host-specific, not for image)
venv/
env/

# Node.js — Don't copy frontend dependencies (huge, host-specific)
node_modules/          # Host node_modules (image will npm ci)
frontend/node_modules/ # Frontend host modules
frontend/.next/        # Next.js build output (host, not for image)
frontend/out/          # Next.js export

# Environment — Don't copy secrets (security!)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local  # All env files (contain secrets)

# IDE — Don't copy editor configs
.idea/    # JetBrains
.vscode/  # VS Code
*.swp     # Vim swap
*.swo
*~        # Backup files

# OS — Don't copy OS junk
.DS_Store    # macOS
Thumbs.db    # Windows

# Docker — Don't copy Docker files themselves (avoid recursion, but keep main Dockerfile)
docker-compose.yml  # Compose file (not needed in image, for host)
Dockerfile*         # All Dockerfiles
!Dockerfile         # Exception: BUT keep main Dockerfile (needed for reference, though not strictly)
Dockerfile.nginx    # Nginx Dockerfile (also excluded, but we keep it via !Dockerfile? Actually this line re-excludes it)

# Data & Logs — Don't copy runtime data (should be volumes, not in image)
logs/     # Logs (ephemeral, via volume)
data/     # Data (via volume)
uploads/  # Uploads (via volume)
*.log     # All log files

# Docs — Don't copy docs (except README)
docs/     # Documentation
*.md      # All markdown
!README.md  # Exception: Keep README.md (useful in image for reference)

# 💡 LEARNER TIP: .dockerignore vs .gitignore
#   - .gitignore: What git ignores (for version control)
#   - .dockerignore: What Docker ignores (for image build)
#   They overlap but are different! .dockerignore should be MORE restrictive.
#   Check what's ignored: docker build . --progress=plain 2>&1 | grep "COPY"
#   Or: docker builder prune && docker build . (clean build, see context size)
